THIRD-PARTY CODE IN qvto-runtime
================================

qvto-runtime is licensed under the Eclipse Public License 2.0 (see the repository's LICENSE). It
reproduces the behaviour of Eclipse OCL, Eclipse QVTo and the Java class library. The following
files port or adapt third-party code or data.

1. Eclipse OCL (classic) 3.22 and Eclipse QVTo 3.11
   Source:    reference/eclipse-ocl, reference/eclipse-qvto (see reference/README.md)
   Copyright: IBM, Borland Software, Open Canarias, Willink Transformations and others
   Licence:   Eclipse Public License 2.0
   Used in:
   - src/coll/ops.rs: ports of org.eclipse.ocl.util.CollectionUtil and of QVTo's
     SetTypeOperations, CollectionTypeOperations, OrderedSetTypeOperations handlers.
   - src/coll/mod.rs: semantics of org.eclipse.ocl.util.BagImpl (iteration, equals, hashCode).
   - src/eq.rs: ports of org.eclipse.ocl.util.ObjectUtil.equal/hashCode; AbstractTuple.
   - src/num.rs: arithmetic of org.eclipse.ocl.EvaluationVisitorImpl and NumberUtil.
   - src/strings.rs: string operations of EvaluationVisitorImpl and QVTo's StringOperations.
   - src/display.rs: toString of AbstractTuple, CollectionUtil, DictionaryImpl.
   - src/dict.rs: DictionaryImpl, MutableListImpl.

2. SimOxide (same author, EPL-2.0)
   Source:    simoxide/crates/simoxide-testkit/src/javafmt.rs, simoxide-sim/src/javahash.rs
   Used in:   src/java/fmt.rs (Double.toString, adapted and extended to Float.toString),
              src/java/hash.rs (String.hashCode).

3. Java class library behaviour (OpenJDK 21)
   No OpenJDK source is copied. src/java/hashmap.rs reimplements the documented behaviour of
   java.util.HashMap (table sizing, resize split, tree bins as red-black trees with the
   comparison rules of HashMap) and is checked against the JDK by tests/differential.rs.
   src/java/chars_data.rs is data generated from the JDK's java.lang.Character by
   tools/oracle/GenChars.java (Unicode character properties, Unicode licence for the data).
